.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt MTREE 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mtree
.Nd format of a file hierarchy specification
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An
.Nm
specification describes a file hierarchy, one entry per line: a path, then
keywords of the form
.Ar keyword Ns = Ns Ar value .
A line beginning with
.Ql #
is a comment, and a line ending in
.Ql \e
continues on the next.
The system's dist sets are described by specifications in
.Pa /etc/mtree ,
and
.Xr makefs 8
builds images from them.
.Pp
A path containing a
.Ql /
is a full path from the root of the hierarchy, beginning
.Ql ./ ,
and
.Ql \&.
is the root itself.
A path without one is relative to the current directory: an entry of
.Cm type Ns = Ns Cm dir
makes itself the current directory, and the line
.Ql ..
returns to its parent.
.Pp
In a path, a space, a byte outside printable ASCII, and any of
.Ql # ,
.Ql \e ,
.Ql * ,
.Ql \&? ,
.Ql \&[
and
.Ql =
are written as
.Ql \e
and three octal digits.
.Pp
Two commands set defaults for the entries after them:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm /set Ar keyword Ns = Ns Ar value ...
Each entry gets these keywords unless it has its own.
.It Cm /unset Ar keyword ... | Cm all
Removes defaults.
.El
.Pp
The keywords are:
.Bl -tag -width sha256digest
.It Cm contents
Where a file's contents are, for
.Xr makefs 8 .
.It Cm gid , Cm gname
The group, by number or name.
.It Cm link
A symbolic link's target, encoded as a path is.
.It Cm mode
The permission bits, in octal.
.It Cm sha256digest
The SHA-256 digest of a file's contents
.Pq also Cm sha256 .
.It Cm size
A file's size in bytes.
.It Cm time
The modification time, as
.Sm off
.Ar seconds . Ar nanoseconds .
.Sm on
.It Cm type
.Cm file ,
.Cm dir ,
.Cm link ,
.Cm char ,
.Cm block ,
.Cm fifo
or
.Cm socket .
.It Cm uid , Cm uname
The owner, by number or name.
.El
.Pp
Other keywords are kept and ignored.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/mtree -compact
.It Pa /etc/mtree
The installed sets' specifications.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr makefs 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
format first appeared with the
.Nm mtree
utility in
.Bx 4.3 Reno .
